  "sections": {
    "intro": "Poem -4\nI see myself play the character everyday even when i type this, it's a complete character. That is behaving exactly the way he is supposed to. I can already see the ending and i am not happy w",
    "Suddenly i love myself, i feel myself changing and i absolutely love this new me. A guy who is not scared to talk to girls anymore. A guy who looks good. A guy people love to be around. I have opened a lot these past few days, i am instilled with extreme energy and am talking non stop. I am not the quiet depressed person who makes a circle on a white paper and lives in it, now i choose to see the world colourfully. I Savor every moment, every person and every interaction and learn from it. I am happy now. So yeah, I've made new friends apparently i made friends with divyanshu's gf and am trying to overcome this gynophobia shit. I kinda hard crushing over this girl called aishwarya who funny enough turned out to be a bisexual. But i don't know why I still feel some sort of connection with her. I dream about her and stuff. This time it's not like dia it's serious, I am ready to go take to her in-person and sober. I want her her in my life and i absolutely believe it's going to happen. But the thing i don't know what to talk to her and if it may come out as cringe. Another funny thing the whole college is behind her. Anyways, I've started to put out my \"intellectual\" thoughts and darshan seems to actually understand what i am saying....i have told these thoughts to soo many people yet they don't understand. This guy does, i see a long term friendship which probably end up being short. It's crazy like just when you are loving something, God takes it away from you. I am suddenly starting to feel and enjoy college life and it is on the verge of being over. All these memories, all these learnings. Before i loved school now i love college more. I become a completely different person tomorrow. I am going a responsible person cause my job starts tomorrow. I will start earning. Do i want to do the job? Hmm maybe yes.... I've come to terms with myself. No way of living is the right way of living. The way you are living your life is the right way. I don't care about money man, i just want to be happy . I will try my best in the job and all. These insomniac nights brought me here. Well since i am here let me tell you a story of friendships. Like i connected with rishabh in that November month when we were alone. I connected with darshan when we both caught for sneaking in alcohol and i saved his asss or wait maybe it's now that he understands my thoughts. I connected with ashutosh when he was roomate and when i fought with him for South movies and he made me realise my ego. I connected with divyanshu when he included me man or when he called me when i was at home... Like no one from this gang did, it maybe for some work but it's his way of showing he remembers you..... Whatever. Funny enough i connected with dushyant too the day he decided to open up after a session of highness. I connected with Akshay on my birthday when we discussed how toxic our group was. It's amazing how the group evolved man. College is not about the place, it's about the people. My family is pretty happy, i got placed. Life's happy man, this is probably the only happy note in this my life series cause i feel like writing only when i am sad and stuff. Anyways crazy how i started the year depressed after going to a trip with basically unknown people, OH and tick that bucket list cause i went on a trip with strangers and girls. Yah boi, i haven't talked properly to any of those girls but alright. This trip put me in an extremely uncomfortable zone and made me normal. I can now easily talk to girls and stuff but man that phase was hard. The surviving and adapting part. The whole trip i was quiet cause this motherfucking selfish guy rishabh decides to bring his gf along. I talked to the guys well and actually people are remembering memories of that trip with me in it now. So that trip, i think i may forget it so let me put it down. It started with rishabh going along with those people and slowly sliding me in too. These fuckers decided to drive 500km on a car which tired the fuck out of me, the whole one way trip i was sitting pretty uncomfortably beside rishabhs gf aaarushi like literally at one point i could feel her ass on my thigh or something. This fucking couple kept kissing and were completely indulged in each other. The others guy's just went to tell their lame selfish stories about themselves. I was pretty high for most of the trip so it flowed by. The main reason i went on this trip even tho i could've gone with divyanshu was rishabh and getting myself out of my comfort zone. I was just hoping rishabh stayed by side and i slide into that grp. But well he didn't and i kinda felt lonely even with all those people. I enjoyed and loved the scenario's and hated the photo sessions. I was so dumb and shy that i failed to get my pictures in a lot of which i looked good. Maybe i don't deserve good pictures or God wants me to forget this trip. So the new year started unlike any other year with no celebration, countdown, loud music or even close friends or family. We were high and we called. I was agitated af man, i was craving for some kind of ALCOHOLIC HIGH AND DANCE. Then the next day i decided to change, i started talking a Lil bit more. While coming back i ditched rishabh and ended up in a all boys car and enjoyed that part. We literally sat and started dancing on the bonnet of the car. Even the midnight last day drive with me, shreyas,ishika and rishabh was really fun. We were high af and in the dark night just parked our car in a shady place and took a walk. This part was where i was adapting. It's not like the guys or girls are badd, evryone on that trip where good people even the girls but i couldn't man. I want something else and was scared too. Well it made me realise afterwards that in fact going to that trip was a good choice. I released all that i vented up on the trip as soon as I got back to hostel. I was unleashed man, controlled and calm but filled with energy. From they day till now i am still going on with that energy. Who knows maybe this is MY YEAR. Anyways excelsior!": "Myself and insta\nJust like voldemort our ancestors if they were to come back or be born again to gain all their knowledge back they have stored it in art.\n\nI am a confident charming person that people",
    "I've realized after the trip. A lot of things. About how everything is a choice. I talked to my sister a lot and i realized i forgot about a person all together. I've become this person i hate. Where did it all go wrong i wonder and i realized it was the weed. It made me forget everything. It made the world bleak as hell. I have come to realisation that it completely destroyed me. I let it. When people talk about the cons of weed it's not just about it. It made my life so miserable . All this while I've been depressed over nothing . No break up or heart break. Nothing. It was this shit. It made my mind so fucked up that i stopped and forgot a part of me . That person that went to rich ass school like Glendale. Man i lost who i am completely. Even the first 2 days of the trip was depressing and bad cause i was too high before leaving for the trip. Now i realize what trap i was in. Happiness was a choice all along. Where did the guy go.. What was i running away from. I literally stopped talking to my sister bruh. The only person that was with me all along and knew all my stories. What kind of person have i become. But bruh addiction is so bad.. Every single time i look to fall on it. It's so scary to run away when it's sitting in my cupboard. At least here in hyd, i am in my house and shit but in Bangalore i got no where to run. I don't know man it filled my world with darkness. Drugs are bad. Don't let anyone tell you otherwise. It's been 3-4 years of continuous...i mean there were 2-2 weeks or months breaks. But i was an addict. I choose to look elsewhere for answers for my pain when it was in front of my eyes all along.": "Bro Rushil iss dharti ke neeche ek duniya hai. Uss dharti ke bahar ek duniya. Tera andar ek duniya hai. Iss reeth mai ek duniya hai. Kaha kho gaya tha tu. Welcome back Rushil. Wake up. Stop the addict",
    "Man it was 11th class...i am 23 now ... He just touched me..  i am kind of over it now.... After the trip after touching the hand of a girl": "After going to Bangalore... The first day is going to be so hard....i might lose the game\n\nMy biggest fear is home sickness. Always has been. It's cause of this shit that i started and continued to do",
    "I wonder why i live in the worst imagination possible when the imagination in people's head is so crazy. I have nothing to be happy about. I went to solo trip and i realized that happiness is a choice. Everything is a planned dopamine hit....i forced myself to be good. I tried to do things after my trip that i would rarely do. I found joy in some yet i continue to be broken. Even after faking my smile and running towards something different. I feel alone and empty. Something ain't right. Plus the demons i fight everyday. One demon tells me to masturbate another to smoke up. I know they are killing me. But i want to die. I see no joy in living. I tell myself that just by existing we can change the world. You can be nothing and still change the world by being alive. I tell myself of the demons everyone fight with everyday. Every grown up lives brokenly. Learning to live brokenly without giving up is the ultimate test. Yet i don't understand what's the point. What's at the end of all this. More pain. I know this pain is just in is starting stages. I told myself aasu pelenge. We can do it. Yet the tears never stop. The world gives me more reasons to be sad than to be happy. Everyday i wake up to nothing. No joy, nothing to await. I looked at the nature for inspiration and all it gave me was jealousy. I despise these trees and the birds for not having a concious mind. I wish i could shoot a bullet in my head to stop thinking. I wish i could be like the rest that don't think much. Don't see much. Yet i can't. I feel maybe it's cause of the girls. Maybe being a 23 year old that never kissed a girl is the problem. Not getting what the age or the body demands is pushing me to be this way. But it's just a reason. I know that once i get a girl the pain gets even more worse. My eyes might open even more and I'd see something darker. I am happy my top of mountain is easy to climb yet i refuse to climb it cause once i am top i would see the other mountains. I don't understand how people live 50 years in this world. Maybe i can't handle emotions. Maybe i am but good at lying to myself. I know for a fact that i am capable of many things but sulk in agony in a corner. It's a race, always been a race. Yet i refuse to run. I am player and the audience. I see the game from afar and it doesn't interest me yet i am the player that is waiting to go to the next level. Why does God give me so much pain. I also wonder whether this is pain. People survived holocaust and torture. What is my pain compared to them. Yet i only know of the mountain i see in front of me. I fight an invisible war. I know everyone is fighting too. I see it in their eyes. The innocent dark eyes of my toy poodle, i see it in him too. Unable to speak, fighting to be happy. Yet all these people have a master. My master turned out to be fragile. Convincing myself that my pain is greater than anything in the world is the worst thing a man can do to himself. So i try looking away. Yet everywhere i see patterns and it bores me. Everything is predictable. Everything is sad. I stich my mask with metal nails yet the blood never lets it stay on. I made sure very less people see what's inside. I hid well. Yet i can't hide from myself. This bastard in me always chooses pain. Even in happiest of moments he detaches me and shows me the moment from a third person view and it hurts. Maybe it's the images of happiness that I constructed in my head that draw me into this well of darkness. These images are very hard to reach everyday. I am weak. I choose to fall rather than fight and climb. I love my thoughts and my brain too much to ignore whatever it feeds me. How can I be happy in this world i wonder. I can't do things everyday that make me happy. Maybe i need to turn into a slave to something. I need to give my chains to someone so i can walk around. Obey it. Find happiness in his happiness. Aasu peena ka liya aasu aa bhi nhi rha. Mera dard mera ki kisi aur ka. Yeh dil dhadakta hai, ya chidiya khil khilate hai aur mai ghirte rahtha hu. Sab dhadakan ka ek hi awaaz hai tho koi kyu nahi Mera saat. Kyu ya dil akela. Mera parchai kyu nhi deti mujhe khushi. Zinda hu yaar kaafi hai. Par Zindagi sa karu kya. Iss maidaan mai ek pattar jiski koi value nahi. Ya duniya agar mil bhi jaaye tho kya hai": "The problem is not weed ... Never been weed. But the dependency of my mind on it. My earning to numb my thoughts. That was the problem all along.",
    "Literally bro all my life i never held the hand of a girl of a stranger. They have soft and small hands. It was great feeling walking into a beach of water holding her hand. I had no intentions involved . I found out there that armu guys swim 20km from ross island to port blair. I was ashtonshid. Anyways then we went to a well and used to bucket to get water from a bucket and washed ourselves. Then we went home. You see i could've called manoj bhai too for the swim but I didn't . I lied as well to her just to get this experience. I did it. Fuck the world. What i realized is that i try to change according to people and i change myself so much that i become the person the other guy wants to me to be. In this process i become attached which I shouldn't. You see even here before i met the girl, we had formed a boys gang. We were planning to get drunk and shit. I couldn't gone that route, but this is a route i always take. I went way past my comfort zone. Smashed it and kept talking to your girl. Just the smell of chut is hypnotizing.. throughtout the trip i could've gone to a spa gotten handjob..i had full capacity. Money. Everything. But i didn't go by choice. I've realized that i am better. Even I'm my life I've become a kid and force myself to become a kid to my parents. They way want me to be. I am stuck always trying to be liked. I cut parts of me which obviously i don't fully leave. But i cut them to pertain to people. I find joy in it. Being a person that nobody complains or has problems with. You see all the fights with me was cause of the other person. Akshay guy my head with a ring but even after all that i still talk to him like old times. Even the next day i talked to him saying how is your finger. You see after we got drunk i instigated him. I mean we went in a lift. There is a tap rule which he did not do. So i acted like i am punching him in the groin but bro literally slapped me hard. Then when i came out there was a ringing sound so i went and slapped him not as hard as he did. And called it equal. Throughtout the car we were shouting at each other. When we reached the house....i was removing my shoes and bro hit me in the back of head with a ring. I Could've died. This was just days before my Europe trip. I got stitches bruh. This guy went inside and with guilt broke his finger. My stitches were 5 days and he got fracture... He has a CAT EXAM A to write which he was preparing hard. I was actually so angry that i was about to throw apot at him but i stopped myself. Line i always do. Even in 9th grade when a person was being very rude to me. I lifted a chair to hit him but stopped mid air and before I put it down he held the chair. Then after started teasing saying how he stopped me and shit. I always stop me myself. I never let my emotions get the best of me.. You see that's the problem in my life. I never go out of my way to be with a girl cause i don't care. I feel they are boring and shit. But yeah man. Anyways finally me, manoj and krthika went to the airport in the same auto. Now i am flight and i think. It was one of the best trips of my life. I would love to do it all again. This time I'll open up more. Talk more.. I've realized the potential i have, the deep conversations ....i can make. It's just immaculate yet my overthinking and stuff. Stop me. People complement e my English and my Hindi. I speak like a local guy. Bruh like i said your pain disappears. You remember only what you want to remember and you want others to remember. You can craft a perspective so crazy that only you will like. You see trying to be the friends of my chappri friends I've lost some sides of me that i noticed again in the trip. I thought i am a loser and people see me that way. But the power of my clothes and my face and my hairstyle was there all along. I can't see my own face. But the way others talk to me just changes man. People feel happy and privileged just to talk to me.i became so fixated in my head man.. i never wanted to be like this. But after watching so many movies and you know my understanding goes beyond anything. Through this process i by mistakenly crafted a narravtive where everyone are like me. They feel things like i do. But it's way different. I thought people are smart in a way. I am very good at assessing people but i am too early to judge and i get scared that people also judge metoo fast. Which is why i am scared always tu be in the eyes of people. I am scared of them cause i can exactly estimat the image of me in their head. Cause i know exactly what i am putting forward. I constrained MYSELF by being attached. I need to be free. You see i sat with this ranchi guy Rakesh and while i was talking to him. I felt these are my friends here. I felt the same feeling when i talked to my friends. You see even when i was talking to the girl. He was trying to interrupt. He was calling me to eat with him like my friends do. I didn't go. I stayed with the girl. But yeah man talking to him i felt how it's the same everywhere. I can get the same shit i am getting.. Elsewhere. I might also get better stuff. But somehow i am too scared to let go. I dwindle back to the same old people. I make an effort once and when i get people i settle. I see talking to people as a task but as a routine. I feel i need the energy to talk to people. I never put in the energy tho. I do it by choice but very rarely. I have that face mann... Can't escape it. I have to break the barrier first. Then they will instantly talk to me. Yet i put the effort once. Attach to people and act as if i am settled. I don't why but i find peace in settling. Even in my life my parents are pushing for me to be settled and it am bending. I am scared of people. But i know for a fact that godd gives someone something and it will eventually be used oneday. It's like the cherkovs gun . Everything has a purpose that will eventually show up. In the grand scheme of things this small dust might change the universe. Also i puked in a ferry. I tried and forced myself not to puke cause i Would lose my aura points and was scared people will judge me. But i did anyways. Cool. That was it. I somehow had no less peace cause i didn't have the time to note stuff down. Now that i did i feel peace. I've realized i love love writing. Bruh that Billy was smoking beedis...🤣... Funny thing is i will never know the repercussions of the relationships i made. I might have been a creep in someone's head. Like bruh billy's craziest experience is that he shot a riffle.": "",
    "What God has planned for you nothing can stop it.. this is the first thing i wrote in my Andaman trip diary. I read it on an auto when I've arrived and i noted it down.": "",
    "But yeah man i came back from the trip and i find it scary to tell people about my amazing experience. I feel they will feel jealous and behave differently with me. These days cause of social media and everything it has become a competitive world. Everyone is going through so many emotions yet no one to talk to. There is this sense of loneliness in everyone. We were trained to run behind sustainability that now we are wanting randomness  craving for the next random thing to be entertained by. It's a fucking goat parade. If you want to be part of the goats you have to mehh. If they think i am a tiger. I am dead. I kinda feel more loneliness At home then i felt there. I think i lost myself in the trip. I somehow can't back to being normal.": "Like a short story is coming to my mind. Like an animal with legs walkss and then sees a sad animal with a single leg. Then this animal cuts off it's own leg and both start laughing together. Then oth",
    "Was this person always inside... YES. Then why was he hiding. Why did he focus more on his pain and forget other's pain. ... Do i have the confidence this time to let this person breathe? Or am i still scared? Do people like aanand and bawarchi.. Those happy people spreading happiness and shit exist in real life... Can i be them . Can i hold him. I used to be that person as a kid but the people around me and their taunts and the wrath in their eyes just submerged me.  I was very hyped guy as a kid i used to do the randomest of things for fun. But that person slowly died. I've seen him in that trip but not fully. He was still scared to come out. There is something huge sitting on him. .... Amidst all this...i wonder will i live up to my name- Rushil(charming)": "The word rushil means charming na?? Am i right.... That hyped kid would do what i did this morning. He woke up early took the dog to walk and talked to people on road .. Didn't think about the people ",
    "Andaman trip": "What God has planned for you nothing can stop it\n\nWhat do people do in life in general? Like i came to beach and then i don't know what to do. I mean it's just a beach. Like abhi kya karu. Then i am l",
    "I've realized we are serving images. I can tell everyone this trip was amazing maybe it is. But maybe i can hype it. Add lies that aren't actually lies. I can tell everyone I've turtles in my scuba. I've talked to foreigners I've made friends. Yet i haven't. I did talk to people but is that the whole truth. Yet the people see images. Not the whole truth. Even if i did tell the truth they would only serve the image in their heads. Not the truth. So what is even the truth. I've talked to a person that is forced to take over his father's business. Recently married a girl he does not like. He is always stressed at his business. He has no choice. I do. Yet what even am i doing.": "Rushil Rushil Rushil Rishi Reddy whatever why are you scared of people. You know i came here to Andaman thinking i will be a different person. I thought in this place where no one knows me, where noth",
    "Jaane wo kaise log tha jinka pyaar ko pyaar Mila. Hum na jab kaliya maangi kaaton ka haal mila. Aaaa. Hum na tho jab kaliya mangi katooon ka haaal mila. Jaane wo kaise log tha ki jinka pyaar ko pyaar mila. This is my life. I've accepted it. But my heart still earns for love. I've realized that i am disrupting man. I seek pain in happiness. I will never be happy. I am too aware of this world. It's people. Their wants. Jeena mehanga hai maut sasti. I think i am free now. You know i used to think it's me. I am not going outside or i am not doing things to attract people. I did those things yet no one notices me. Maybe i am always meant to be alone. Aasu pelenge. It's alright. You see i listen to and heard stories where a girl enters randomly in their life and they seize the opportunity. I never get the opportunity. I am god's lonely man. Everywhere i go i attract loneliness. I've seen a solo girl traveller and i tried to approach her. Yet i didn't get the chance. I try to talk to people. I try to make friends. Yet i rarely get the chance. I am not an introvert. The world made me. I know how to talk to people. How to make them like me. I've seen it. Yet i never get the chance. My job is in a team that only has oldies. My section is a place where there aren't any girls available for me. I've realized my pain is biological. I am a hopeless romantic. I seek love. Yet i don't get any. Everywhere i go it's just use. Use and throw. I never come across people that want to talk to me. Want to call me. Yes my family is there. I love them. Yet there is no anyone else. Every friend I've made i have given them countless love. Yet all i received was pain. I am too scared to show emotions. I am scared to show my desperation. I feel this is a race and it is a race. So i drink my tears. I hide my feelings. I have shown my feelings to people yet all i received was betrayal at every point of my life. Maybe i am meant to be broken. You know everything I go to a temple i wish for my family to be happy. Cause they are the only ones in this world that care about me. Sometimes i wonder what if they aren't there. What if they leave. How will i survive in this world. I don't know. I've realized this pain will just grow and keep on growing. I've made countless dating apps. Texted random people. I tried everything within my reach. I always do. If i see an opportunity i don't miss. I run. Me crying in the above paragraph is alright but i never lose hope. I keep trying. Trying till i fall. Yet i never get anything. You see i could have gone to a spa and cummed on a girl's face. Given i am 23 and never touched a girl. This would have been a start for me and positively broken the barrier. But i still couldn't bring myself to do it. I don't know why. You see i did go in search of a spa today but it was full. Everytime I try i don't get anything. I used to think my past lover cursed me. Now i am starting to belive in it. In my head i want to fuck many girls but maybe i am a woman man. Boring. She might cheat me or have multiple boyfriends before me. But i will never. I don't know why but i feel one day i will marry a girl and the love will be beyond anything I've ever imagined. It will fulfill all my desires. But she will leave early. I heard from my mom that when my jatakam was checked out was written this way. The world is preparing for me to be alone. Cause come on Man. Solo trip. Europe trip. A job. College. No where have i at least gotten close to a girl. I had crushes but on the wrong people. I've realized it in the process that they aren't meant for me. So i never tried. I am serious they seriously aren't for me. Everyone around me told that. They are tooooooo short or sometimes they are lesbian. I never found someone that was at least 10% for me... So that i could seize the opportunity. I am not a introvert or a scared person. If i truly want something i take it. But i need hints. You see yesterday in something different. I went to smoke a cigarette and a person sat in front of me but before i could speak to him he left. I again went to smoke and he was there. This time i talked to him. Plus he did like talking to me. It's all about opportunity. A small hint or maybe a circumstance out of nowhere. I never got it. You know even if it wasn't meant for me i would grab it but i do need something man. I never got it. You know tamasha is my fav film and learnt the dialogues cause i thought maybe it might happen to me. I learnt \"Mai apna naam bataunga, tum apna bateyegi. Hum ek doosra ko jaan jaayenge. Common friends nikal aayenge. Aur mai phir whi banuga jo mai saal bhar ban ke rahta hu. Whi ghissipitta jokes sunaunga. Decently behave karunga. DECENTLY BEHAVE KARUNGA. Yahi corsica Mai. Jaha mujhe koi nahi jaanta, mai koi bhi ho saktahu, kuch bhi kar sakta hu, kisi ki paddi nahi... DON. Baara mulko ki police mujhe dhoond rahi hai aur iss anjaan island mai teja ka sone dhoondhne nikla hu\". I memorized it. Yet i never got the chance. Even last time when i went to anirudh concert all alone. I cried on the way back home. It was the next concert I've ever been to. Yet i was all alone. It was a party. It was crazy. I loved listening to his music live. Which is why i went there in the first place. But also i thought maybe i will find a girl. I never did. I went to lifafa concert. This was indoors in a club with alcohol. I didn't find it here as well. Even after so much pain . So much brokeness. Even though i knew what would happen to me in the trip. I still booked it. I knew what my trip was going to be. I didn't want to come. Yet i still did. With the hope of finding something. Like always i never did. Just pain. I go to so many movies alone. I book a seat in a place beside someone single. In hope that maybe. Maybe i find a girl. Yet it never happens. Even when it does. I don't get the opportunity to talk. Like imagine a girl sat beside me in a movie theatre and get phone fell down. I would help and then talk. I never got they opportunity. Even with a broken heart. I am brave enough to break it again. I am happy to face pain. Yet all i get is pain. Last week before the trip i called everyone i knew in college and talked to them. Hanged out with them. But all I got was pain. Even when i writting such a serious note god sends mosquitos to buzz in my ear. I am maybe meant to be single forever. This is it. My life. You know people that knew guru dutt always said he was depressed and in pain and that is why his art is what it is. You see all the films he made are classics now but they flopped when they released. Even his last film which he put his whole soul into. Flopped. He left movies. Died like a kafka. Maybe i am kafka or i want to be. Maybe i want to make something that is worthy of this pain. Yet even on the job side i am just bored. Plain. Everywhere i go i just get pain. Even at the restaurant i went yesterday. Every restaurant i go i hope there is a chance yet i get none. I keep trying the randomest of things. Board games, DND, cinema clubs. Yet never.": "Bruh bruh bruh it suddenly rained here and i ordered local andaman fish and it's probably the best dish i ever ate. It was just amazing. The salt and masala was just perfect. The fish and the aloo ble",
    "After taking 1 hour with my parents i feel i will remember this trip differently. The last night in havelock really changed things. People really don't think at my level. I am not saying this cause i am extreme or something. But in general. I know for a certain fact that i think in a way that very rarely people do. My perspective is going to change. This true Trip will be remembered differently cause of different people. It's an achievement I've haven't yet understood. I will later. I will think about this trip and wonder how i managed to this shit. I am Rushil after all. All this pain doesn't matter. Cause i choose to remember it differently. I am havelock the first day went to radhanagar beach. Then i came back with a bottle. The next day i got a scooty and went to kala patthar beach. Brought a magnet. Went to something different. Drank cocktails. Talked to a random person. Then next day i went to a private resort and enjoyed private radhanagar beach did a forest trek and then I came back and put a towel and enjoyed private time at my place at Vijay Nagar beach. Explored the sea life. Scorpions and shit. I drank the whole bottle and ate the best dinner ever. I had the best drive on scooty. Alone. All these thoughts won't matter anymore. It rained. The final moments change everything. Fuck it. Fuck people. Fuck girls. I have lived the best trip ever. My extreme depression is just fruit of me. It will obviously always be there unless i surround myself with low level thinkers. I only choose to look at the girls that stated at me with pride and jealousy as i sat alone with phone and my food. Fuck everything else. It's my perspective. My life. I will tell lies to burn people. I will make them feel jealous. My instagram stories are doing the job. Fuck my depression. Drinking alcohol or loving someone changes everything. This is my bitter chrysalis.": "Maybe i have a serious face. People are scared to talk to me. I need to initiate the conversation but i rarely do. \n\nBilly. Damnn i met a \n\nI judge people way too early. It's crazy man. Last day at zo",
    "Bruh the last day was a ride. I arrived in zostel and met with this crazy dude that has pet snake. He was there for scuba course 8 days and bro saw turtles and stingrays and snakes. He builds educational spaces and works with an NGO. He was also an animal rescuer. Bro just holds snakes for fun. He got his binoculars and we did bird watching and shit. Then i met a foreigner who i had a very long conversation with. He was from UK but his mom is from India but born in UK.. Bruh is the same age as me. He was a kayaking consultant. And many other boats. This guy had travelled more India then me. He almost been to b40 countries. He did 2 years job and left the job and if just travelling. One place to another. Bro i was confused cause before he opened his mouth i thought he was Indian.. He used to code in CAPL and earned a lot. Bruh went to Delhi in diwali. He was like he was scared and bored of life.. How it feels written. So he is traveling. He sold his car and house and everything to be here. He was going to Thailand next.. This guy literally took a bike to rotung la pass. All alone. He was in a tent in Himalayas. I talked to him for 1.5 hr and was astonished and mind blown. He told me craziest experience he had in all trips was almost falling off a cliff. Bruh played football in Kerala and some metal went into his foot. Plus he solo. The coolest person I've ever met.": "",
    "Then i went to cellular Jail all alone and you know what 's very interesting is the tree that no one noticed. It must be a 100 years old and touching it transported me to the age of sarvakar. I then came back and met with a guy from Kerala who is just 22 and works as ground staff for indigo. This guy can literally travel anywhere around the world in just 1700 rs round trip. I met a person from Ranchi who was just like my college friends. This guy was a Tata aiq health insurance guy. He handles a region. Bruh was also so tired of job and was angry that no one of friends was coming to trip. So he came alone. First time. Then i met manoj Teja who was a business consultant .. Pretty old like 34 and was still unmarried and roaming solo. It was so great talking to him. Then wait for it ..i initiated a conversation with a girl.. krithika all by myself. MYSELF. Bruh. I said hi and we started talking.. She told me how she was in havelock and some random auto guy took her number saying I'll help in you scuba. Then he started texting stuff like baby i miss you and shit. Did video calls late at night. She almost filed an fir on him.. then we mingle with the bigger gang. Everyone started talking and talking. This girl was kinda dumb in a fun way. She was touching me and putting her feet close to me. Saying Mera muh mai paani chale gaye. Showing her skin and feet and saying. Dekh kitna tan ho gaya. Feet par scratches aa gaye and shit. She is an architect and a journalist. She has he individual practical. She is 29. Then we played uno... My suggestion. I explained everyone the rules... No one knew how to play. We play like 4 games and slept. It was fun. This krithika was like Mai harr roz beach mai swimming kari and the next day was her last day as well. So she was like swimming Chalo to me in the morning 6. Mujhe utha do aake. Bruh i went to swimming with a girl. Throughtout this trip i never went inside the sea.. Like mostly feet. But man I wasn't able to sleep properly cause of this shit. Like i was thinking will she come or will we kiss at least. Will i say my tamasha dialogue. But i thought to myself keep expectations low. Don't think of getting involved it approaching. So bro in the morning i went to her room with all boys. I woke her up and we went to swimming. While walking into the beach i held her hand. That was it. I am not saying i like the girl or love and shit. But i held the girl": "",
